    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0653" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-31T16:00:00+02:00">January 31, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 1—3:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>354. In the course of my visit of condolence over the death of General
                        Metaxas<anchor n="14a" xml:id="d605-f1"/> the Greek Minister here informed
                    me that German officials, both military and civil, were utilizing every
                    opportunity and contact to assert to him the precarious situation of Greece,
                    specifically <pb facs="0654" n="642" xml:id="pg642"/> alleging that American
                    help would not be forthcoming in time to be effective and that American planes
                    and other armament were inferior to German.</p>
                <p>The German officials had not, I understand, gone so far in their representations
                    to him as to suggest that the Greek Government endeavor to make peace with Italy
                    but it was obvious that they hoped he would believe and repeat to Athens these
                    defeatist ideas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d605-f1" n="14a" xml:id="d605-f1-content">
                <p>General Metaxas died January 29, 1941.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
